    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Basics"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Start with the fundamentals to build a strong foundation:"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "numbered-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**What is LINQ** \u2014 Understand what LINQ is and its purpose",
          "**Why LINQ** \u2014 Learn the advantages of LINQ over traditional approaches",
          "**LINQ API** \u2014 Explore the .NET API architecture for LINQ",
          "**LINQ Query Syntax** \u2014 Learn the SQL-like query syntax",
          "**LINQ Method Syntax** \u2014 Learn the fluent method syntax",
          "**Lambda Expressions** \u2014 Understand the building blocks of LINQ methods"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Standard Query Operators"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Master the standard query operators, which are the core methods that make up LINQ:"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Filtering"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**Where** \u2014 Filter elements based on a predicate",
          "**OfType** \u2014 Filter elements based on type"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Sorting"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**OrderBy / OrderByDescending** \u2014 Sort elements in ascending or descending order",
          "**ThenBy / ThenByDescending** \u2014 Secondary sorting"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Grouping"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**GroupBy** \u2014 Group elements by a key",
          "**ToLookup** \u2014 Create a lookup dictionary"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Joining"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**Join** \u2014 Inner join two sequences",
          "**GroupJoin** \u2014 Group join (left outer join equivalent)"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Projection"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**Select** \u2014 Transform elements",
          "**SelectMany** \u2014 Flatten nested collections"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Aggregation"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**Aggregate** \u2014 Custom accumulation",
          "**Average** \u2014 Calculate average",
          "**Count** \u2014 Count elements",
          "**Max** \u2014 Find maximum value",
          "**Min** \u2014 Find minimum value",
          "**Sum** \u2014 Calculate sum"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Quantifiers"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**All** \u2014 Check if all elements satisfy a condition",
          "**Any** \u2014 Check if any element satisfies a condition",
          "**Contains** \u2014 Check if collection contains a value"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Element Operators"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**ElementAt / ElementAtOrDefault** \u2014 Get element at index",
          "**First / FirstOrDefault** \u2014 Get first element",
          "**Last / LastOrDefault** \u2014 Get last element",
          "**Single / SingleOrDefault** \u2014 Get single element"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Set Operations"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**Distinct** \u2014 Remove duplicates",
          "**Except** \u2014 Set difference",
          "**Intersect** \u2014 Set intersection",
          "**Union** \u2014 Set union"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Partitioning"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**Skip / SkipWhile** \u2014 Skip elements",
          "**Take / TakeWhile** \u2014 Take elements"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Other Operators"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**Concat** \u2014 Concatenate sequences",
          "**SequenceEqual** \u2014 Compare sequences for equality",
          "**DefaultIfEmpty** \u2014 Handle empty collections",
          "**Empty / Range / Repeat** \u2014 Generate collections",
          "**Conversion Operators** \u2014 Convert between types"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Advanced Concepts"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**Expression Trees** \u2014 Understand how LINQ providers translate queries",
          "**Deferred Execution** \u2014 Learn when queries execute",
          "**Immediate Execution** \u2014 Force query execution"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "summary-box",
